    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Epigastric pain on naproxen (R10.13)</content>. Dyspepsia from near-daily naproxen, possibly with gastritis or a small ulcer; no alarm features (no bleeding, anemia, vomiting, dysphagia or weight loss), hemoglobin 15.0 g/dL today against 15.2 at intake, and he is under 60, so endoscopy is not needed now. Helicobacter pylori should be tested and treated if present. The pain is not cardiac in character. Near-daily naproxen went beyond the as-needed plan and was not caught at the preventive visit two weeks ago. [S]<list><item>Stop naproxen; no ibuprofen, aspirin or other oral anti-inflammatories.</item><item>Omeprazole 20 mg each morning before breakfast for four weeks.</item><item>Helicobacter pylori stool antigen: the sample was collected here today, before the first omeprazole dose.</item><item>Diclofenac gel on the thumb may continue, as little is absorbed.</item><item>Return at once for black stools, vomiting blood, fainting or severe pain.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic low back pain (M54.59)</content>. Mild now; he can manage without naproxen. [S]<list><item>Heat and his physical therapy exercises; acetaminophen is of little help for back pain and is not prescribed.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Noninvasive Treatments for Acute, Subacute, and Chronic Low Back Pain: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2017); ACG and CAG Clinical Guideline: Management of Dyspepsia (2017)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review at the eight-week visit next week. Stool antigen result by phone. Next scheduled visit 1956-09-29: eight-week review: back pain after six weeks of physical therapy, the thumb splint, the stomach after stopping naproxen, weight and blood pressure. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>
